# Work lifecycle

Full detail: `AGENTS.md`, sections "Where things live" and "Work lifecycle". Issues, milestones and PRs live on Gitea (`APESCIC/NPO.WorkDash` at `gitea.intranet.apes.org.uk`, the `origin` remote); use `tea` from inside the clone. GitHub issues are turned off.

Before the first edit:

1. Find the issue (`tea issues ls --keyword "..."`) or create one with a `[Epic]`, `[Story]`, `[Task]`, `[Bug]` or `[Chore]` title prefix, the matching label, area labels, and the usual body sections (Summary, Context / why, Scope, Acceptance criteria, Out of scope, Dependencies):

   ```powershell
   tea issues create --title "[Task] ..." --description-file <body.md> --labels "task,devops" --milestone "v0.3.0 SaaS core"
   ```

2. Milestones are named after their release (`tea milestones ls`). Link the issue under its parent by making the parent depend on it, so the parent cannot close first:

   ```powershell
   tea api -X POST "/repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/<parent>/dependencies" -f owner=APESCIC -f repo=NPO.WorkDash -F index=<child>
   ```

3. Branch from `main`: `cursor/{feature|fix|chore}/<issue>-<slug>`. Never commit to `main`.

While working:

- Comment on the issue (`tea comment <n> "..."`) for decisions, blockers, scope changes and when the PR opens.
- Split large work into linked child issues instead of growing one issue.
- Tick acceptance criteria as they are met.

When finished:

- Close the leaf issue with a comment linking the PR and release.
- Close a parent only when all its children are closed.
- Check the milestone's open/closed count (`tea milestones ls`).
